nk, and the tree is removed\nba7c6961 test: a copy is deleted whatever modes the code run in it left on its directories, and the double of a refused preparation's suite that closed a directory is deleted while IH-04 is asked with its survey\na79eedb6 docs: the four defects of the reading of kernel refusals are recorded fixed by the launch that no longer reads the system log\n6c7d3072 docs: the registry records that no test holds the survey's walk without links, its unreadable directory nor the deletion of its copy, and an unrun race of a leftover process under bubblewrap\n3ab89027 refactor: the judgement and the survey of a prepared suite run on a disposable copy of the reference and its files set up and deleted in one place\n0828bb00 refactor: the profile of a surveyed run and the paths it wrote are decided beside the listing of the copy, keeping the control runner under four hundred lines\n0e36ee97 docs: the registry no longer records defects of the reading of kernel refusals, that reading being gone\n19bfed16 feat: the IH-04 asked after refused preparations offers grant_writable from the paths their suite wrote on a disposable copy, naming the control and the first-level directories and citing those paths, the writes the kernel refused being gone from the observation, the evidence and the preparation record\nb77c4ebc test: after refused preparations whose suite creates test-output/run/a and tries to write outside the copy, IH-04 offers grant_writable for test-output/ to the unit control citing the surveyed paths and nothing for the outside path, and offers it not when the suite writes nothing\nd16b47a5 feat: a refused preparation has its suite run once more on a disposable copy of the reference and its files where it may write, and its record keeps under suite_written the control and the paths written there, less those already given to the control; a retained preparation does not run its suite again\n16c264cf test: the record of a refused preparation carries test